{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795628885,"nonce":"6yb6VDozc1/MFOGLf/s4GZRsi6Q=","title":"Code editor: after a fold, the caret, current line and selection are on the wrong rows","message":"Reported by use: after collapsing a block, a press puts the cursor on the right line but the caret is drawn below it.\n\nThe current-line box, the selection and the caret were placed at `line_index * line_height`, which counts the hidden lines. Press hit testing already mapped rows to lines. The same fault in other places:\n- a drag mapped the pointer to a line index, not a shown line, and ignored the gutter when only folding was on;\n- scrolling the caret into view and the content height counted hidden lines;\n- arrow, word and page keys moved the cursor into hidden lines;\n- `folded_regions` stayed at its line numbers as lines were inserted or removed above, hiding the wrong lines.\n\nFix: folding and the row mapping move to `widgets/code/fold.rs`; everything places by row; movement skips hidden lines; after an edit the folds move with the text and a fold whose braces no longer pair is opened; a cursor landing in a hidden line opens it.\n\nTests: `blinc_layout/tests/code_folding.rs`, `blinc_recorder/tests/code_folding.rs`.","files":null}]}